window.WIKI_PAGES = [{"slug": "Agni", "title": "Agni, Lord of the Black Flame", "keywords": "# Agni, Lord of the Black Flame\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Agni, Lord of the Black Flame](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/agni.png)\n\n| Skill data | Agni, Lord of the Black Flame |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Ultimate Skill |\n| Inspiration | Nu Udra |\n| Combat role | Tentacle pulls / burning ground |\n| Active modes | 3 |\n| Toggleable passive | Furnace Mantle |\n| Passive upkeep | 60 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:agni` |\n| Previous | [Black Flame](Black-Flame.md) |\n| Evolution | \u2014 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Alma", "title": "Alma", "keywords": "# Alma\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| NPC data | Alma |\n| --- | --- |\n| Origin | Monster Hunter Wilds |\n| Race | [Awakened Hunter](Awakened-Hunter.md) |\n| Entity | `wildhunt:alma` |\n| System | Native Tensura Otherworlder |\n| Skin | Bundled original 64\u00d764 classic Minecraft skin |\n\n![Gemma and Alma in the Minecraft client](../media/alma-gemma.png)\n\n## Character\n\nAlma is the expedition handler and researcher. Her skin follows the dark hair, round glasses, rust expedition coat and cream hood of her base appearance.\n\n## Tensura abilities\n\n| Ability | Registry ID | Character fit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Analyst | `tensura:analyst` | Field research and analysis |\n| Observer | `tensura:observer` | Watch monster behavior and the environment |\n| Analytical Appraisal | `tensura:analytical_appraisal` | Identify specimens and equipment |\n| Thought Acceleration | `tensura:thought_acceleration` | Process findings quickly |\n| Danger Sense | `tensura:danger_sense` | Warn the expedition |\n| Magic Sense | `tensura:magic_sense` | Read unfamiliar energy |\n| Multilayer Barrier | `tensura:multilayer_barrier` | Protect herself during fieldwork |\n\nThese are real Tensura abilities learned and toggled through native entity-existence data. They use Tensura's effects, passive logic and available NPC behavior. A native humanoid AI handles movement, hostility, melee and subordinate commands; a player-only UI or manual mode of a skill does not gain an invented autonomous AI here. The race also grants Hunter's Recovery as a separate racial Extra Skill.\n\n## Spawning and otherworlder behavior\n\nAlma participates in Tensura's **otherworlder spawn distribution**, including its natural otherworlder replacement and summon selection. The eight regular native entries and these two hunters have equal 0.10 weights; the total remains 1. Special Shizu/Hinata rolls and the native overall spawn chance are unchanged. A datapack can override these distributions and loadouts.\n\nUse `/summon wildhunt:alma` or `/give @s wildhunt:alma_spawn_egg` for a direct check. Native otherworlder ownership, inventory, home handling, interaction menus and configured Unique-skill drops are inherited. Races, skills and equipment persist through native saving; loading never reinitializes them. Their native entity data supplies 160,000 aura / 80,000 magicules before any applicable modifiers.\n\n## Front hairline correction in 0.7.2\n\nAlma's front hairline now uses a short, even fringe above a narrow forehead. The large triangular gap on the front is removed. This correction changes only the top four pixel rows of the front head face; her glasses, eyes, nose, mouth, other head faces and outfit are preserved.\n\n![Alma front hairline in Minecraft 0.7.2](../media/alma-front-hairline-072.png)\n\n## Skin correction in 0.7.1\n\nThe top, side and rear head textures now use a separate opaque atlas. This removes Gemma's black patch and gives Alma a coherent swept-back hairstyle. The existing front faces, clothing and equipment pixels are preserved.\n\n![Corrected rear head textures in Minecraft 0.7.1](../media/otherworlder-hair-rear-071.png)\n\n## Visual reference and skin provenance\n\nAppearance reference: [Monster Hunter Wilds Alma page](https://monsterhunterwilds.wiki.fextralife.com/Alma). Common skin libraries blocked automated downloads during development, so this is an **original generated and UV-packed interpretation**, not a downloaded community skin or a ripped game texture. The character reference images are not redistributed in this repository. Source art and reproducible nearest-neighbor UV packing are in `art/` and `scripts/prepare-skins.py`.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Otherworlders \u00b7 Version 0.7.2\n"}, {"slug": "Apex-Hunter", "title": "Apex Hunter", "keywords": "# Apex Hunter\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| Race data | Apex Hunter |\n| --- | --- |\n| Family | Human / Hunter |\n| Stage | 2 of 3 |\n| Appearance | Human |\n| Previous | [Awakened Hunter](Awakened-Hunter.md) |\n| Next | [Sovereign Hunter](Sovereign-Hunter.md) |\n| Base EP gate | 400,000 |\n| Distinct bosses | 3 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Aura-Regeneration", "title": "Aura regeneration", "keywords": "# Aura regeneration\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| Skill data | Hunter recovery Extra Skills |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Extra |\n| Acquisition | Hunter race evolution; no permanent magicule acquisition cost |\n| Activation | Native toggle; new racial tier enabled automatically |\n| Resource | Aura only |\n| Idle cost | None at full applicable health |\n\n## Recovery tiers\n\n| Extra Skill | Race | Native inspiration | Healing | Aura cost |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Hunter's Recovery | Awakened Hunter | Self Regeneration | 4 HP/second; 8 mastered | 20 per HP |\n| Apex Renewal | Apex Hunter | Ultraspeed Regeneration | Missing HP every half second | 30 per HP; 20 mastered |\n| Sovereign Rebirth | Sovereign Hunter | Infinite Regeneration | Missing HP and SHP every half second | 30 per HP / 10 per SHP; 20 / 5 mastered |\n\nRegistry IDs: `wildhunt:hunters_recovery`, `wildhunt:apex_renewal`, `wildhunt:sovereign_rebirth`.\n\nOnly the strongest **toggled** aura recovery tier works. Earlier skills stay learned and can be used if you turn a stronger one off. Recovery uses only available aura and heals proportionately if you cannot afford all missing health. HP is funded before SHP. Full health costs nothing. Mastery increases only on a funded recovery, and existing skill mastery is preserved.\n\n## Native integration and limits\n\nAll three are native Extra Skills, granted through Tensura's racial skill learning system. Their icons reference native regeneration icons at runtime. They do not apply native regeneration effects that would charge magicules on a later tick.\n\nHealing respects native severance maximum HP and interaction suppression. Hunter's Recovery and Apex Renewal also respect native healing suppression such as Frost and Curse. Like native Infinite Regeneration, Sovereign Rebirth can recover through ordinary Curse, Frost and strong Black Burn, but Infinite Imprisonment prevents it.\n\nSovereign Rebirth can stop an ordinary lethal hit by paying 30 aura (20 mastered) to preserve 1 HP; subsequent half-second recovery pays for the remaining healing. It cannot stop invulnerability-bypassing damage, barrier bypass level 1.75 or higher, complete severance, spiritual-health depletion, suppressed interactions or an unfunded recovery. It does not grant free immortality or spend magicules. Repeated lethal hits must each be funded.\n\n## Energy split\n\nHunter base evolution energy is split **2/3 aura and 1/3 magicules**. Tensura's default alignment also gives kill EP in that 2:1 ratio; native gain bonuses, penalties and server caps still apply. Spending aura does not transfer EP, change maximum magicules, or alter the allocation of later gains.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Extra Skills \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Awakened-Hunter", "title": "Awakened Hunter", "keywords": "# Awakened Hunter\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| Race data | Awakened Hunter |\n| --- | --- |\n| Family | Human / Hunter |\n| Stage | 1 of 3 |\n| Appearance | Human |\n| Previous | Human |\n| Next | [Apex Hunter](Apex-Hunter.md) |\n| Base EP gate | 100,000 |\n| Distinct bosses | 1 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Black-Flame", "title": "Black Flame", "keywords": "# Black Flame\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Black Flame](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/black_flame.png)\n\n| Skill data | Black Flame |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Unique Skill |\n| Inspiration | Nu Udra |\n| Combat role | Tentacle pulls / burning ground |\n| Active modes | 2 |\n| Toggleable passive | Furnace Mantle |\n| Passive upkeep | 15 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:black_flame` |\n| Previous | \u2014 |\n| Evolution | [Agni, Lord of the Black Flame](Agni.md) |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Commands", "title": "Commands", "keywords": "# Commands\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\nAll commands affect the issuing player. No operator permission is required, and progression gates are still enforced.\n\n| Command | Function |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/wildhunt` or `/wildhunt guide` | Show the brief gameplay guide |\n| `/wildhunt status` | Show race stage, base EP, distinct boss IDs, mastery and learned-art resources |\n| `/wildhunt evolve` | Advance one hunter stage if eligible |\n| `/wildhunt ascend rey_dau` | Evolve mastered Storm Crown into Raijin |\n| `/wildhunt ascend uth_duna` | Evolve mastered Scarlet Deluge into Varuna |\n| `/wildhunt ascend nu_udra` | Evolve mastered Black Flame into Agni |\n| `/wildhunt ascend jin_dahaad` | Evolve mastered Frostbound Colossus into Ymir |\n\n## Passive status\n\nEach learned art reports its passive name, ON/OFF state and aura upkeep per second. Use the native skill toggle in Tensura\u2019s Ability Selection to change that state. Status does not grant resources or change a toggle.\n\n## Ascension requirements\n\nBe Sovereign Hunter, retain at least two million base EP, own the matching Unique, and master it. The new Ultimate is learned before its source Unique is removed. Failed eligibility checks do not consume your source skill. There is no trial requirement.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Evolution", "title": "Human evolution", "keywords": "# Human evolution\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\nThe alternate branch is **Human \u2192 Awakened Hunter \u2192 Apex Hunter \u2192 Sovereign Hunter**. Every stage keeps a human appearance. The base Human\u2019s original Tensura evolution choices remain available.\n\n| Stage | Previous | Base EP | Distinct bosses | Additional requirement |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| [Awakened Hunter](Awakened-Hunter.md) | Human | 100,000 | 1 | \u2014 |\n| [Apex Hunter](Apex-Hunter.md) | Awakened Hunter | 400,000 | 3 | \u2014 |\n| [Sovereign Hunter](Sovereign-Hunter.md) | Apex Hunter | 2,000,000 | 5 | Master one apex Unique skill |\n\n## HP and SHP growth\n\n| Stage | HP bonus | SHP bonus | HP gained from previous hunter stage | SHP gained from previous hunter stage |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Awakened Hunter | +100 | +400 | +100 | +400 |\n| Apex Hunter | +500 | +3,200 | +400 | +2,800 |\n| Sovereign Hunter | +1,000 | +6,600 | +500 | +3,400 |\n\nThese are bonuses to the underlying maximums, not total health values. They use native HP and `MAX_SPIRITUAL_HEALTH` attributes. Evolution replaces the previous race modifiers instead of stacking them. Login upgrades existing hunter maximums while preserving current HP and SHP; it does not refill them.\n\n## Balance reference\n\nTensura 2.0.1.3 defaults give Enlightened Human +80 HP/+300 SHP at 100K EP, Human Saint +480/+3,000 at 400K EP plus four boss kills, and Divine Human +980/+6,000 at 2M EP. Hunters keep the same EP gates but require distinct boss types (and mastery at the final stage). Their bonuses stay near this curve, with a modest premium for those constraints. Sovereign's 1,020 base total HP stays below Minecraft's default 1,024 attribute cap.\n\n## Aura recovery and EP\n\nEach stage automatically grants a new [aura regeneration Extra Skill](Aura-Regeneration.md): Hunter's Recovery \u2192 Apex Renewal \u2192 Sovereign Rebirth. Only the strongest toggled tier heals; earlier ones remain in the ability menu.\n\nNative evolution energy floors are 200K / 800K / 2M total EP, split **2/3 aura, 1/3 magicules**. Default alignment already has a 2\u00d7 aura and 1\u00d7 magicule kill-EP multiplier; this addon preserves that native calculation, gain bonuses, player penalties and server caps. It does not convert existing saved magicules into aura or touch unrelated races.\n\n## Distinct boss kills\n\nThe record counts **boss entity types**, not individual spawns. Ten Wither kills give one entry. Wither plus Ender Dragon gives two. Credit is cumulative, survives death and requires a player-attributed kill while Human or a hunter.\n\nEligible types are listed in `wildhunt:progression_bosses`: the shared `c:bosses` tag (including Tensura\u2019s bosses), Wither and Ender Dragon. Future Monster Hunter mobs can be added by datapack. Ordinary hostile mobs do not count.\n\n## Evolving\n\nUse Tensura\u2019s evolution menu or `/wildhunt evolve` after meeting the same gates. Check `/wildhunt status` for the recorded type IDs, base EP and mastery progress. Skill acquisition is independent: bosses never award the four Unique skills.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Frostbound-Colossus", "title": "Frostbound Colossus", "keywords": "# Frostbound Colossus\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Frostbound Colossus](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/frostbound_colossus.png)\n\n| Skill data | Frostbound Colossus |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Unique Skill |\n| Inspiration | Jin Dahaad |\n| Combat role | Avalanche impact / capture / ice siege |\n| Active modes | 2 |\n| Toggleable passive | Colossus Carapace |\n| Passive upkeep | 20 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:frostbound_colossus` |\n| Previous | \u2014 |\n| Evolution | [Ymir, Lord of Winter](Ymir.md) |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Gemma", "title": "Gemma", "keywords": "# Gemma\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| NPC data | Gemma |\n| --- | --- |\n| Origin | Monster Hunter Wilds |\n| Race | [Awakened Hunter](Awakened-Hunter.md) |\n| Entity | `wildhunt:gemma` |\n| System | Native Tensura Otherworlder |\n| Skin | Bundled original 64\u00d764 classic Minecraft skin |\n\n![Gemma and Alma in the Minecraft client](../media/alma-gemma.png)\n\n## Character\n\nGemma is the expedition smith. Her skin follows the blonde hair, goggles, cropped brown jacket, cream top, utility belt and ochre work trousers of her base appearance.\n\n## Tensura abilities\n\n| Ability | Registry ID | Character fit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Godly Craftsman | `tensura:godly_craftsman` | Forge and improve equipment |\n| Analytical Appraisal | `tensura:analytical_appraisal` | Judge materials and weapon quality |\n| All Seeing Eye | `tensura:all_seeing_eye` | Spot fine defects |\n| Strengthen Body | `tensura:strengthen_body` | Handle heavy tools |\n| Steel Strength | `tensura:steel_strength` | Support physical smithing work |\n| Flame Manipulation | `tensura:flame_manipulation` | Control forge heat |\n| Ultraspeed Regeneration | `tensura:ultraspeed_regeneration` | Recover from workshop and field injuries |\n\nThese are real Tensura abilities learned and toggled through native entity-existence data. They use Tensura's effects, passive logic and available NPC behavior. A native humanoid AI handles movement, hostility, melee and subordinate commands; a player-only UI or manual mode of a skill does not gain an invented autonomous AI here. The race also grants Hunter's Recovery as a separate racial Extra Skill.\n\n## Spawning and otherworlder behavior\n\nGemma participates in Tensura's **otherworlder spawn distribution**, including its natural otherworlder replacement and summon selection. The eight regular native entries and these two hunters have equal 0.10 weights; the total remains 1. Special Shizu/Hinata rolls and the native overall spawn chance are unchanged. A datapack can override these distributions and loadouts.\n\nUse `/summon wildhunt:gemma` or `/give @s wildhunt:gemma_spawn_egg` for a direct check. Native otherworlder ownership, inventory, home handling, interaction menus and configured Unique-skill drops are inherited. Races, skills and equipment persist through native saving; loading never reinitializes them. Their native entity data supplies 160,000 aura / 80,000 magicules before any applicable modifiers.\n\n## Skin correction in 0.7.1\n\nThe top, side and rear head textures now use a separate opaque atlas. This removes Gemma's black patch and gives Alma a coherent swept-back hairstyle. The existing front faces, clothing and equipment pixels are preserved.\n\n![Corrected rear head textures in Minecraft 0.7.1](../media/otherworlder-hair-rear-071.png)\n\n## Visual reference and skin provenance\n\nAppearance reference: [Monster Hunter Wilds Gemma page](https://monsterhunterwilds.wiki.fextralife.com/Gemma). Common skin libraries blocked automated downloads during development, so this is an **original generated and UV-packed interpretation**, not a downloaded community skin or a ripped game texture. The character reference images are not redistributed in this repository. Source art and reproducible nearest-neighbor UV packing are in `art/` and `scripts/prepare-skins.py`.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Otherworlders \u00b7 Version 0.7.1\n"}, {"slug": "Getting-Started", "title": "Getting started", "keywords": "# Getting started\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Minecraft 1.21.1 and Java 21.\n- NeoForge 21.1.209 or newer in the 21.1 line.\n- Tensura: Reincarnated 2.0.1.3, ManasCore 4.0.0.2, Architectury and Tensura\u2019s required GeckoLib, SmartBrainLib and TerraBlender dependencies.\n- Wild Hunt 0.7.2 installed on both client and server.\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload the 0.7.2 addon from the repository\u2019s `releases` directory. Replace older Wild Hunt jars; do not load two versions together. The addon jar is not a complete modpack.\n\n## First reincarnation\n\nComplete Tensura\u2019s ordinary reincarnation flow. The four apex Uniques are eligible starting rolls alongside the server\u2019s configured pool. A particular apex skill is not guaranteed. Existing rolled skills remain valid after upgrading.\n\n## First hunter evolution\n\nStay Human, grow to 100K base EP, and defeat one eligible boss type. Select Awakened Hunter in the evolution menu or use `/wildhunt evolve`. Race progression and skill rolling are independent.\n\n## Choosing a playstyle\n\nChoose [Storm Crown](Storm-Crown.md) for ricochets and mobility, [Scarlet Deluge](Scarlet-Deluge.md) for currents and native barriers, [Black Flame](Black-Flame.md) for visible tentacle pulls and burning ground, or [Frostbound Colossus](Frostbound-Colossus.md) for avalanche impacts and ice capture.\n\nEach skill has a separate toggleable passive in Tensura\u2019s Ability Selection. Toggle it on for sustained benefits while paying aura upkeep. It is no longer the last active buff mode. Mastery improves damage; EP does not supply an addon damage multiplier.\n\n## In-game help\n\n`/wildhunt guide` explains progression. `/wildhunt status` shows base EP, distinct boss IDs, mastery and passive status. [Command reference](Commands.md).\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.2\n"}, {"slug": "Mechanics", "title": "Combat mechanics", "keywords": "# Combat mechanics\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n## Damage and mastery\n\nWild Hunt\u2019s damage multiplier is:\n\n```text\n0.90 \u00d7 (1 + 0.5 \u00d7 clamp(masteryFraction, 0, 1)) \u00d7 (Ultimate ? 3 : 1)\n```\n\n**No EP term is present.** After the 10% damage reduction, mastery caps at 1.35\u00d7 the old Unique raw base, or 4.05\u00d7 that base for a mastered Ultimate. The reduction also covers every area pulse, counter and signature impact. Skill-page tables already include the Ultimate\u2019s 3\u00d7 multiplier. Native Tensura elemental boosts, global combat rules, rank interactions, barriers and resistances still apply; raw values do not promise the same health damage against every enemy.\n\nEP remains a requirement for race evolution and Ultimate ascension. Those progression gates do not increase these attacks\u2019 raw damage.\n\n## No passive stacks\n\nStorm charge, owned oil stacks and owned rime stacks are removed. No attack builds, consumes or amplifies damage from them. Old marks are ignored and removed as entities tick. There is no shatter threshold or melee coating.\n\nOil pools remain finite **world locations**, not passive stacks on a character. Drenched remains one timed water mark: it has no counter or buildup and supports the documented water/lightning interactions.\n\n## Toggleable passives\n\nEach skill has two active modes (three for an Ultimate) plus a separate native skill toggle in Tensura\u2019s Ability Selection. The old final buff modes are removed from mode cycling.\n\n| Line | Passive | Unique aura / second | Ultimate aura / second |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Rey Dau | Storm Mantle | 10 | 40 |\n| Uth Duna | Water Veil | 10 | 40 |\n| Nu Udra | Furnace Mantle | 15 | 60 |\n| Jin Dahaad | Colossus Carapace | 20 | 80 |\n\nThe first second is paid when enabling; upkeep is charged once every twenty game ticks while active. Passives stay on until disabled, unfunded or blocked by activation requirements. They do not expire after fifteen or thirty seconds. Attribute contributions use stable IDs, so refreshes cannot accumulate duplicate bonuses. Turning off or forgetting the skill removes its modifiers. Saved native toggle state is restored on login.\n\n## Native barriers\n\nWater Veil and Colossus Carapace contribute to Tensura\u2019s `PHYSICAL_BARRIER` and `MAGIC_BARRIER` attributes and now arm `MULTILAYER_BARRIER`, which is the attribute read by its shield HUD counter. Tensura handles their interaction with damage and renders its native barrier layer around the character. Wild Hunt adds no absorption hearts and does not implement a parallel shield-health pool. Other skills\u2019 barrier contributions remain separate.\n\n| Passive | Unique capacity | Ultimate capacity |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Water Veil | 100 | 250 |\n| Colossus Carapace | 150 | 350 |\n\nThe displayed value is native per-hit blocking capacity. Tensura charges magicules for blocked damage. Overflow, inadequate magicules and native power interactions can break the shield. A broken multilayer barrier automatically rearms at the first paid upkeep after ten seconds without a hit (normally 10\u201311 seconds). Hits, including fully blocked hits, restart recovery. Retoggling cannot skip this delay. The shield modifier is saved across relogs; turning off removes only this art\u2019s contribution. Ensure Tensura\u2019s **Barrier** HUD decoration is enabled if you have customized its HUD.\n\nWater Veil retains water breathing and an attacker-targeted retaliation after actual health damage. Furnace Mantle retains fire protection while enabled; both utility effects stop immediately on toggle-off without leftover timed potions. Furnace Mantle no longer oils melee victims. The old frost ward\u2019s projectile deletion and interception budget are removed.\n\n## Aiming and movement\n\nRailbolt begins with a block-clipped aimed hit, then ricochets from the latest victim. Thunder Step follows the full aim vector, including vertical pitch, and sweeps the whole caster bounding box. Collisions, build-height limits and the world border stop it. Railbolt bounces reach twelve blocks through walls from the most recent victim. Thunder Step reaches 16/24 blocks with a 5/4 second cooldown and preserves all three components of player momentum. Undertow is placed on the crosshair ray within 24/36 blocks, using the hit surface or bounded endpoint. Water waves sweep continuous segments so targets cannot hide between movement updates. Oil Lash selects a limited forward fan and creates synced tentacle geometry. Avalanche Crash is an aimed area impact; Glacial Prison targets one enemy. Heavenfall Glacier warns fixed positions for half a second before impact.\n\nAttacks respect teams, owned pets, creative/spectator immunity and PvP settings. They check line of sight except for Railbolt ricochets after the initial hit. Movement respects knockback resistance. Dimension changes invalidate anchored effects. Native status resistance and skill ranks can prevent Frost or Chill. No art destroys terrain or places permanent ice.\n\n## Aura regeneration\n\nSee [Aura regeneration](Aura-Regeneration.md) for the three race-granted Extra Skills, healing speed, aura costs, suppression and death-prevention limits. They never charge magicules. Default native EP gain stays split two thirds aura and one third magicules.\n\n## Visual effects\n\nWater waves render a broad curled mesh with a foam crest; Undertow renders rotating teal and coral spiral ribbons. Water and ice toggles emit no constant custom particles. Oil Lash uses a synced procedural mesh with a dark tapered body, glowing orange bands, extension and recoil, including on a miss. Ice spires, prison bars and falling ice use rendered faceted crystals. Those visual entities deal no damage by themselves, have no collision and expire automatically; server skill logic owns targeting and damage.\n\nTensura supplies elemental particles, shockwaves, native barrier rendering and animated magic circles. Its assets are used at runtime and are not copied into the addon.\n\n## Barrier HUD examples\n\n![Water Veil native HUD showing 100](../media/water-veil-hud.png)\n\n![Colossus Carapace native HUD showing 150](../media/colossus-carapace-hud.png)\n\nCaptured with the Unique passives enabled in the Minecraft development client, Wild Hunt 0.6.0.\n\n![Centered portraits and combined native barrier HUD](../media/hunter-icons-and-barriers.png)\n\nWild Hunt 0.7.0: centered Rey Dau, Uth Duna and Jin Dahaad portraits. The native HUD shows 250 combined capacity with both Unique barrier passives enabled (100 Water Veil + 150 Colossus Carapace); no custom bubble/frost orbit is emitted.\n\n## Hunter vitality\n\nRace HP bonuses are +100 / +500 / +1,000; native SHP bonuses are +400 / +3,200 / +6,600. These replace earlier hunter-stage bonuses. Existing saved hunters get the updated caps on login without being healed. See [Human evolution](Evolution.md#hp-and-shp-growth).\n\n## Updating saved characters\n\nVersion 0.7.0 refreshes race vitality on login, grants missing racial regeneration skills, and leaves current HP/SHP unchanged. Barrier cooldowns and surviving shield state remain saved.\n\n\nVersion 0.5.0 introduced the mode migration and keeps learned skills, mastery and distinct boss history. It removes old transient combat timers and resources, drops the old buff mode, and moves the former fourth Ultimate mode into the third active slot while preserving/capping its cooldown. Equipped presets migrate with the mode list. When upgrading from pre-0.5.0 combat, legacy toggle passives start off; no skill reroll is needed. A matching still-active legacy Water Veil absorption effect is cleared during migration. Version 0.6.0 added native HUD barriers to already-enabled passives on login and refreshes hunter HP/SHP modifiers; existing toggle state, mastery and boss history remain intact.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Raijin", "title": "Raijin, Lord of Thunder", "keywords": "# Raijin, Lord of Thunder\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Raijin, Lord of Thunder](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/raijin.png)\n\n| Skill data | Raijin, Lord of Thunder |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Ultimate Skill |\n| Inspiration | Rey Dau |\n| Combat role | Ricochet lightning / mobility |\n| Active modes | 3 |\n| Toggleable passive | Storm Mantle |\n| Passive upkeep | 40 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:raijin` |\n| Previous | [Storm Crown](Storm-Crown.md) |\n| Evolution | \u2014 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Scarlet-Deluge", "title": "Scarlet Deluge", "keywords": "# Scarlet Deluge\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Scarlet Deluge](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/scarlet_deluge.png)\n\n| Skill data | Scarlet Deluge |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Unique Skill |\n| Inspiration | Uth Duna |\n| Combat role | Moving tides / native barriers |\n| Active modes | 2 |\n| Toggleable passive | Water Veil |\n| Passive upkeep | 10 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:scarlet_deluge` |\n| Previous | \u2014 |\n| Evolution | [Varuna, Lord of Tides](Varuna.md) |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Skills", "title": "Skills", "keywords": "# Skills\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\nFour rollable Uniques evolve into four Ultimates. Every line has **two active modes plus one toggleable passive**. Each Ultimate adds a **third active signature**.\n\n| Unique | Ultimate | Active arts | Toggleable passive |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [Storm Crown](Storm-Crown.md) | [Raijin](Raijin.md) | Ricochet Railbolt; Thunder Step | Storm Mantle |\n| [Scarlet Deluge](Scarlet-Deluge.md) | [Varuna](Varuna.md) | Travelling wave; aimed whirlpool | Water Veil |\n| [Black Flame](Black-Flame.md) | [Agni](Agni.md) | Rendered Oil Lash; pool ignition | Furnace Mantle |\n| [Frostbound Colossus](Frostbound-Colossus.md) | [Ymir](Ymir.md) | Avalanche Crash; Glacial Prison | Colossus Carapace |\n\n## Obtaining skills\n\nUniques join Tensura\u2019s configured reincarnation primary pool. Rolls remain random. There are no skill trials or skills awarded for boss kills. Ultimates require Sovereign Hunter, two million base EP and mastery of the matching Unique.\n\n## Using skills\n\nEquip and cycle active modes using Tensura\u2019s normal ability interface. Enable the passive with the native skill toggle in **Ability Selection**; it is separate from the active modes. It requires ongoing aura. `/wildhunt status` shows its on/off state and upkeep.\n\n## Power\n\nMastery improves damage by up to 50%; Ultimates use a 3\u00d7 base multiplier. Wild Hunt adds no EP-based damage scaling, charge battery, oil stacks or rime stacks. Read [Combat mechanics](Mechanics.md) for native barrier behavior and migration details.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Sovereign-Hunter", "title": "Sovereign Hunter", "keywords": "# Sovereign Hunter\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n| Race data | Sovereign Hunter |\n| --- | --- |\n| Family | Human / Hunter |\n| Stage | 3 of 3 |\n| Appearance | Human |\n| Previous | [Apex Hunter](Apex-Hunter.md) |\n| Next | \u2014 |\n| Base EP gate | 2,000,000 |\n| Distinct bosses | 5 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Storm-Crown", "title": "Storm Crown", "keywords": "# Storm Crown\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Storm Crown](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/storm_crown.png)\n\n| Skill data | Storm Crown |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Unique Skill |\n| Inspiration | Rey Dau |\n| Combat role | Ricochet lightning / mobility |\n| Active modes | 2 |\n| Toggleable passive | Storm Mantle |\n| Passive upkeep | 10 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:storm_crown` |\n| Previous | \u2014 |\n| Evolution | [Raijin, Lord of Thunder](Raijin.md) |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Varuna", "title": "Varuna, Lord of Tides", "keywords": "# Varuna, Lord of Tides\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Varuna, Lord of Tides](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/varuna.png)\n\n| Skill data | Varuna, Lord of Tides |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Ultimate Skill |\n| Inspiration | Uth Duna |\n| Combat role | Moving tides / native barriers |\n| Active modes | 3 |\n| Toggleable passive | Water Veil |\n| Passive upkeep | 40 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:varuna` |\n| Previous | [Scarlet Deluge](Scarlet-Deluge.md) |\n| Evolution | \u2014 |\n\n"}, {"slug": "Version-History", "title": "Version history", "keywords": "# Version history\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n## 0.7.2 \u2014 Alma front hairline\n\n- Corrected Alma's front hairline: replaced the deep triangular exposed forehead with a short, even fringe and a narrow forehead.\n- Reused ManasCore's native race/skill registrars directly to prevent a constructor-time registry lookup failure.\n- Changed only the upper half of her front head texture. Her glasses, eyes, nose, mouth, remaining head faces, outfit, and Gemma's complete skin are preserved from 0.7.1.\n\n\n## 0.7.1 \u2014 Otherworlder hair corrections\n\n- Replaced Gemma's side, top and back head textures to remove the black cutout artifact.\n- Reworked Alma's hair into a coherent swept-back style with a low bun.\n- Preserved both existing front faces, outfits and equipment pixels exactly.\n- The skin packer now rejects transparent head-face tiles rather than forcing cutouts opaque.\n\n\n## 0.7.0\n\n- Railbolt ricochets ignore blocks after the initial block-clipped shot. Horns and portrait gutters are corrected; each icon is isolated and centered.\n- Thunder Step reaches 16/24 blocks, keeps player momentum, and has 5/4 second cooldowns.\n- All art hits, fields, counters and signatures receive a 10% damage reduction. Physical/magic barrier bonuses fall 10%. Native multilayer barriers recover after ten seconds without a hit while funded and enabled; retoggling cannot bypass recovery.\n- Water and ice toggles stop emitting constant custom particles. Crushing Current gets a curled water mesh; Undertow gets rotating spiral geometry and crosshair placement within 24/36 blocks.\n- Hunter HP bonuses become +100/+500/+1,000; SHP +400/+3,200/+6,600, benchmarked against Enlightened Human/Human Saint/Divine Human.\n- Three race-granted aura regeneration Extra Skills preserve the native 2:1 aura/magicule EP gain split.\n- Alma and Gemma join the native otherworlder distribution as Awakened Hunters, with seven character-fitting Tensura abilities each, native humanoid AI and bundled original skins based on online visual references.\n\n\n## 0.6.0 \u2014 Aim, shield HUD and hunter vitality\n\n- Thunder Step now follows vertical aim as well as horizontal direction, retaining body collision and build-height checks.\n- Extended Railbolt\u2019s hop distance from eight to twelve blocks.\n- Added real native Multilayer Barrier capacities to the water/ice passives so Tensura\u2019s shield HUD counter appears. Native damage, magicule costs and break rules apply; upkeep does not repair a broken shield.\n- Increased hunter HP bonuses to +40 / +100 / +200 and added +20 / +60 / +120 native SHP.\n- Existing hunters receive the updated caps on login; existing enabled passives receive their initial HUD barrier without a reroll.\n\n## 0.5.0 \u2014 Direct combat and toggleable passives\n\n- Removed Storm charge, oil stacks, rime stacks and EP damage scaling.\n- Made Railbolt ricochet sequentially; replaced Fulgurite Array with collision-checked Thunder Step.\n- Removed the last buff mode from all eight skills; added native toggleable passives with ongoing aura upkeep.\n- Replaced absorption hearts with native physical and magic barriers.\n- Added rendered tentacles for Oil Lash and faceted ice geometry.\n- Replaced Jin Dahaad\u2019s fissure/rime/ward/frostfront kit with Avalanche Crash, Glacial Prison, Colossus Carapace and Ymir\u2019s telegraphed Heavenfall Glacier.\n- Preserved race gates, reincarnation rolls, learned skills, mastery, boss history and the centered portraits.\n\n## 0.4.0 \u2014 Distinct arts and wiki\n\n- Centered all eight existing portraits with consistent transparent padding.\n- Replaced shared attack/field behavior with charge-and-rods lightning, a travelling tidal wave and reactive veil, owned oil-pool ignition and melee coating, and ice fissures with finite projectile wards.\n- Gave each Ultimate a signature behavior: targeted judgments, alternating tides, a burning pool network, or an expanding frostfront.\n- Integrated native Tensura particles and animated elemental magic circles.\n- Added this linked wiki and offline visual edition.\n\n## 0.3.0 \u2014 Combat and presentation corrections\n\nCorrected seconds-versus-ticks cooldowns, missing skill names and slow domain timing. Added damage progression, original monster portraits, combo mechanics and native skill-rank damage metadata.\n\n## 0.2.0 \u2014 Reincarnation and distinct bosses\n\nRemoved ordinary hunts and skill trials. Added one/three/five distinct boss gates and rollable reincarnation Uniques.\n\n## 0.1.0 \u2014 Initial prototype\n\nAdded the human hunter branch and the eight skill registrations. Its ordinary-hunt/trial design was superseded. Old hunt totals are not converted into boss credit.\n\n---\n\n**Categories:** Tensura: Wild Hunt \u00b7 Version 0.7.0\n"}, {"slug": "Ymir", "title": "Ymir, Lord of Winter", "keywords": "# Ymir, Lord of Winter\n\n[Main Page](../README.md) \u00b7 [Skills](Skills.md) \u00b7 [Evolution](Evolution.md) \u00b7 [Mechanics](Mechanics.md) \u00b7 [Commands](Commands.md)\n\n![Ymir, Lord of Winter](../../src/main/resources/assets/wildhunt/textures/skill/ymir.png)\n\n| Skill data | Ymir, Lord of Winter |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Ultimate Skill |\n| Inspiration | Jin Dahaad |\n| Combat role | Avalanche impact / capture / ice siege |\n| Active modes | 3 |\n| Toggleable passive | Colossus Carapace |\n| Passive upkeep | 80 aura / second |\n| Registry ID | `wildhunt:ymir` |\n| Previous | [Frostbound Colossus](Frostbound-Colossus.md) |\n| Evolution | \u2014 |\n\n"}];
